    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "BER ratings to follow.\r\n\r\nThis is a unique and exciting opportunity to acquire two residential properties set on approximately 10 acres of land in the highly scenic area of Drum, Belmullet, Co. Mayo, enjoying uninterrupted views across the beautiful Sáilin Harbour."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "The main residence is a well-proportioned four-bedroom home with comprising a kitchen, dining area, and living space, offering comfortable family accommodation. A standout feature is the spacious attic level, which is already fitted with roof light windows and is ready for conversion, presenting excellent potential for additional living space such as extra bedrooms, a home office, or a recreational area.\r\n\r\nThe second property is a newly built old style cottage, structurally complete but requiring internal finishing. This offers a fantastic opportunity for the purchaser to complete to their own taste and specification. The flexibility of having a second dwelling opens up a range of possibilities, including guest accommodation, a holiday let, or long-term rental income.\r\n\r\nBoth properties benefit from elevated views stretching out over Sáilin Harbour, providing a truly tranquil and picturesque setting.\r\n\r\nIdeally located just:\r\n\r\n10 minutes from Belmullet town, with all local amenities\r\n10 minutes from Blacksod Point and its iconic lighthouse\r\nWithin close proximity to the stunning beaches of the Wild Atlantic Way, including Elly Bay and Cross Beach.\r\n\r\nThe lands extending to c.10 acres offer additional value and versatility, suitable for farming, hobby use, or further development potential (subject to planning permission).\r\n\r\nThis is a rare chance to secure a substantial holding in a sought-after coastal location, combining lifestyle, investment, and development potential in one exceptional package.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
